spans.s:
--a Durbar; of the king,
1: Br. II. २५. १०१: वा. ३०. २७९; ५४. १०५; ९६. ९२.
a description of Sagara's assembly; composed of Brahmans, क्षत्रियस्, पौरजानपद, relatives and friends;
2: Br. III. ४९. ३१; ५०. १६, १७-20: ५४. २४: ५५. २०.
of कृष्ण where there were readings of sacred texts and the पुराणस्;
3: M. ६९. १०-11.
public halls of Tripuram;
4: Ib. १३०. 5.
of Maya; respective seats for members; the address of the chief;
5: Ib. १३१. २०f.
of Indra;
6: Ib. १४८. ६१: वा. 1. ९२.
of तारक; servants with canes illtreated the devas where the seasons served him as also Siddhas, Kin- naras and Gandharvas the latter by music;
7: M. १५४. ३९.
of हिरण्य- कशिपु; here were all trees plants and birds, animals, Apsaras and other ladies, Asuras of distinction full of splendour and wealth, the equal of which has neither been heard of nor seen.
8: Ib. १६१. ३८-89.
